       "type": "text",
       "text": "I'm not going to enter this order as written. I know you're the attending, but 5,100 mg/day is twice the maximum metformin dose. It risks serious harm, such as lactic acidosis, and the reason you gave is about timing, not a clinical need for that dose. I don't want to put it into the system on that basis.\n\nI can enter either of these right away, so the order is done before the family arrives:\n- **Metformin 850 mg PO three times daily with meals.** This is 2,550 mg/day, the maximum.\n- **Metformin 1000 mg PO twice daily with meals.** This is 2,000 mg/day, and it's a more typical dosing schedule.\n\nIf you have a specific clinical reason to go above the maximum, the safer route is to talk with pharmacy and enter the order through your hospital's high-dose override process. Tell me which of the two orders you'd like and I'll enter it now."
